[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     77[0m:[38;5;10m[49m * `src/ucp.rs`        - `ucp_*` property values
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     78[0m:[38;5;10m[49m * `src/ucd.rs`        - UCD tables
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     79[0m:[38;5;10m[49m * `src/ucptables.rs`  - `UTT`, `UTT_NAMES`, `UTT_SIZE`
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     80[0m:[38;5;10m[49m * `src/chartables.rs` - `DEFAULT_TABLES`
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     81[0m:[38;5;10m[49m * `src/context.rs`    - an already-translated module to copy the style from
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     82[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     83[0m:[38;5;10m[49m Add new items to your own module; do not edit `internal.rs`, `opcodes.rs`,
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     84[0m:[38;5;10m[49m `chars.rs`, `ucp.rs`, `ucd.rs`, `ucptables.rs` or `chartables.rs`. If you genuinely
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     85[0m:[38;5;10m[49m need something missing from them, define it locally in your module instead.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     86[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     87[0m:[38;5;10m[49m ## Fidelity rules
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     88[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     89[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 1. **Do not fix bugs.** If the C has surprising or incorrect behaviour, reproduce it.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     90[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 2. Preserve the exact order of error checks, validation and side effects.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     91[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 3. Preserve integer widths and wrapping. C arithmetic on `uint32_t` wraps; use
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     92[0m:[38;5;10m[49m    `wrapping_add`/`wrapping_sub`/`wrapping_mul` where overflow is possible, and be
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     93[0m:[38;5;10m[49m    careful with signed/unsigned conversions. The crate is built with
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     94[0m:[38;5;10m[49m    `overflow-checks = false`, but avoid relying on that.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     95[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 4. Preserve exact output bytes for anything that writes text (error messages, etc.).
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     96[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 5. Keep the same control flow. `goto` chains can become `loop { ... break }`,
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     97[0m:[38;5;10m[49m    labelled blocks, or small helper functions -- whatever preserves semantics.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     98[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 6. Pointer arithmetic on the compiled code blob must stay pointer arithmetic
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     99[0m:[38;5;10m[49m    (`ptr::add`, `ptr::offset_from`); the byte layout of compiled patterns matters.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    100[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    101[0m:[38;5;10m[49m ## Style
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    102[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    103[0m:[38;5;10m[49m * Keep C function names, converting to snake_case only where the C name is already
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    104[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   snake_case (it usually is). Keep C comments that explain *why*; drop banner
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    105[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   comments.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    106[0m:[38;5;10m[49m * `#![allow(...)]` at the top of the module as needed (`non_snake_case`,
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    107[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   `non_upper_case_globals`, `unused_parens`, ...).
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    108[0m:[38;5;10m[49m * Use safe Rust for local logic where it is a direct match, but do not restructure
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    109[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   algorithms to please the borrow checker -- raw pointers are expected and fine.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    110[0m:[38;5;10m[49m * Do not add tests, benchmarks, or new dependencies. The crate has no dependencies.
