[?25l[0m[38;5;141m> [0mThe translation is complete and verified. [38;5;10mtranslation/[0m now holds a 45.5k-line Rust crate that builds as a [38;5;10mcdylib[0m and behaves identically to the C build of [38;5;10mc_src/[0m.[0m[0m
[0m[0m
[1mWhat was translated:[22m all of PCRE2 10.48-DEV's 8-bit library — the parser and code generator ([38;5;10mpcre2_compile.c[0m, split across [38;5;10mcompile_tables/compile_parse/compile_branch/compile_scan/compile_class/compile_cgroup/compile.rs[0m), both matchers ([38;5;10mmatch_.rs[0m, [38;5;10mdfa_match.rs[0m), [38;5;10msubstitute[0m, [38;5;10mconvert[0m, [38;5;10mstudy[0m, [38;5;10mauto_possess[0m, [38;5;10mxclass[0m, [38;5;10mserialize[0m, and the smaller API and utility modules. The Unicode/character tables were converted from the C by generator scripts in [38;5;10mtranslation/tools/[0m rather than by hand. [38;5;10mpcre2_jit_compile.c[0m reduces to its non-JIT stubs because the CMake build does not define [38;5;10mSUPPORT_JIT[0m.[0m[0m
[0m[0m
[1mSymbols:[22m the exported set matches the C library exactly — 143 symbols, none missing, none extra. That includes the width-suffix quirks the macros produce: [38;5;10mpcre2_compile_8[0m, [38;5;10m_pcre2_study_8[0m, but [38;5;10m_pcre2_compile_add_name_to_table8[0m and [38;5;10m_pcre2_posix_class_maps8[0m (no underscore before the [38;5;10m8[0m), and [38;5;10m_pcre2_utf8_table1[0m (no suffix at all).[0m[0m
[0m[0m
[1mVerification.[22m I built the C library with its own CMakeLists and compared the two side by side:[0m[0m
[0m[0m
- Compiled byte code is byte-identical. [38;5;10mpcre2_serialize_encode[0m was used to dump the compiled form of every pattern; 3318 pattern/option combinations match exactly.[0m[0m
- Every exported data table matches byte-for-byte (the only differences are relocated function/string pointers inside the default contexts), as do all 23 internal static tables ([38;5;10mescapes[0m, [38;5;10mverbs[0m, [38;5;10mautoposstab[0m, [38;5;10mcoptable[0m, [38;5;10mpoptable[0m, [38;5;10mrep_typ[0m, …) and both error-text tables.[0m[0m
- ~2.9M lines of structured API output identical across compile, match, dfa_match, substring extraction, substitute, convert, serialize, contexts, errors, config, maketables, jit stubs and next_match.[0m[0m
- Targeted stress tests identical: match/depth/heap limits with catastrophic backtracking, 300 capture groups, 60KB subjects, DFA restart and workspace exhaustion, substitution case callouts, name tables, locale-derived tables, serialization round-trips with corrupted data.[0m[0m
- 94k lines of UTF-validity output identical, covering truncated/overlong/surrogate sequences and [38;5;10mPCRE2_MATCH_INVALID_UTF[0m.[0m[0m
- Randomised differential fuzzing: ~840 seeds × 400–600 iterations, ~400k pattern/subject/option combinations, all identical.[0m[0m
[0m[0m
[1mBugs found and fixed during verification[22m (each was a real behavioural divergence): 47 sites where a [38;5;10m&mut PCRE2_SPTR[0m was dereferenced once instead of twice, silently compiling as a pointer-to-integer cast; a missing pointer post-increment when setting [38;5;10mXCL_MAP[0m, which wrote the class flag byte 32 bytes late; [38;5;10mread_number[0m writing its outputs on the early return where C does not; [38;5;10mNOTACHAR[0m entries dropped from a UCD table by the generator; missing implicit NUL terminators on C string literals; the [38;5;10mbralink[0m chain loop nested inside the real-compile branch instead of running in both passes; and [38;5;10mPCRE2_CONFIG_COMPILED_WIDTHS[0m reporting a bit that this build does not set.[0m[0m
[0m[0m
The harness lives in [38;5;10mdifftest/[0m ([38;5;10mdifftest.c[0m, [38;5;10mfuzz.c[0m, [38;5;10mstress.c[0m, [38;5;10mutftest.c[0m, [38;5;10mrun_fuzz.sh[0m) and the table generators and audit scripts in [38;5;10mtranslation/tools/[0m, so any of this can be re-run. [38;5;10mc_src/[0m was not modified.[0m[0m
[0m[0m
One caveat worth stating: 29 build warnings remain, and they are intentional — they flag dead stores and unused variables that exist in the C too, which I kept rather than "tidying" into a behavioural change.[0m[0m
